body:
I think this will always print an error on runtimes that don't support spatial containers. Is this what want? I could imagine it both ways

Usually, we want to silently abort when an extension isn't available, and we expect the app to either gracefully handle the extension being missing, or show its own error to the user. So, to match our implementation of other extensions we'd want this to be something like:

```suggestion
	if (!can_create_spatial_container()) {
		print_verbose("OpenXR: Unable to create spatial container!");
		return;
	}
```

But making an app that uses spatial containers is quite different than a fully immersive one, so maybe we do want to handle things differently for this extension, and always show an error?

